WEBVTT

1
00:00:27.486 --> 00:00:29.196
Your father's in danger.

2
00:00:34.660 --> 00:00:37.204
Special Agent Billie Rand. FBI.

3
00:00:37.996 --> 00:00:39.498
I don't talk to cops.

4
00:00:41.625 --> 00:00:43.210
They're gonna kill him. Lucky.

5
00:00:51.969 --> 00:00:53.262
Here's what I know.

6
00:00:54.805 --> 00:00:57.098
Priscilla buys gas. wholesale.

7
00:00:57.099 --> 00:00:59.226
She doesn't pay state taxes.

8
00:01:00.018 --> 00:01:04.438
She then resells it
through shell companies for full price.

9
00:01:05.022 --> 00:01:06.399
That's what I know.

10
00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:11.196
What I don't have is anything
that connects her to that scam.

11
00:01:13.115 --> 00:01:16.869
What she's very good at
is making other people take the fall.

12
00:01:17.870 --> 00:01:20.080
Guess who the fall guy is.

13
00:01:23.208 --> 00:01:29.005
I have enough to put Cary and John away
for the next ten years.

14
00:01:29.006 --> 00:01:30.757
If that were true.
you would have done it already.

15
00:01:33.010 --> 00:01:34.720
Unless there's a reason that I haven't.

16
00:01:37.973 --> 00:01:39.682
Okay. so you only want Priscilla.

17
00:01:39.683 --> 00:01:41.100
And Whittaker.

18
00:01:41.101 --> 00:01:42.852
And I know you want the same thing.

19
00:01:42.853 --> 00:01:44.271
You don't know anything about what I want.

20
00:01:45.731 --> 00:01:47.023
I know that before this.

21
00:01:47.024 --> 00:01:49.192
you and your father
were strictly small-time.

22
00:01:49.193 --> 00:01:55.781
I know that you know that your daddy
is in over his head with Priscilla.

23
00:01:55.782 --> 00:01:58.994
And I know that you wanna get her out
of his life.

24
00:02:01.330 --> 00:02:02.706
So what would you have me do?

25
00:02:03.665 --> 00:02:06.418
Help me take the bull's-eye
off your father's back.

26
00:02:06.919 --> 00:02:09.921
Putting Priscilla behind bars
may be the only way to keep him safe.

27
00:02:09.922 --> 00:02:11.589
You can't guarantee that.

28
00:02:11.590 --> 00:02:14.843
No. But I can keep him out of prison…

29
00:02:16.136 --> 00:02:18.096
if you help me take her down.

30
00:02:21.934 --> 00:02:23.018
I can't.

31
00:02:24.561 --> 00:02:25.645
No.

32
00:02:25.646 --> 00:02:26.647
You sure?

33
00:02:27.397 --> 00:02:30.359
Yeah. I've been chasing Priscilla.
but I've been watching you.

34
00:02:31.276 --> 00:02:33.445
And all your life. you've been…

35
00:02:37.157 --> 00:02:39.368
…playing the hand you were dealt.

36
00:02:40.494 --> 00:02:43.622
This is an opportunity for you
to get out of this shit.

37
00:02:44.164 --> 00:02:46.208
To play with a fresh deck.

38
00:02:46.750 --> 00:02:48.168
What about Cary?

39
00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:51.672
Depends on how deep he goes.

40
00:02:54.758 --> 00:02:55.843
Full immunity.

41
00:02:57.594 --> 00:03:00.180
For my dad and for Cary or else no deal.

42
00:03:04.017 --> 00:03:05.018
Girl.

43
00:03:07.187 --> 00:03:08.522
You ask for a lot.

44
00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:12.401
So do you.

45
00:04:47.746 --> 00:04:48.914
You're alive.

46
00:04:54.670 --> 00:04:55.671
Good for you.

47
00:04:56.588 --> 00:04:58.047
- Lucky.
- Give me the seed phrase.

48
00:04:58.048 --> 00:04:59.674
Lucky. you gotta listen to me.

49
00:04:59.675 --> 00:05:02.845
No. The seed phrase. Please.

50
00:05:04.012 --> 00:05:06.472
Lucky.
Listen. I need to explain. all right?

51
00:05:06.473 --> 00:05:08.015
Can I… Can I… Can I explain?

52
00:05:08.016 --> 00:05:09.309
Don't!

53
00:05:11.228 --> 00:05:12.229
Fuck.

54
00:05:28.495 --> 00:05:30.747
No. I don't want your fucking ice.

55
00:05:40.424 --> 00:05:44.010
Sorry. I knew you would find me.
I just didn't think it would be this soon.

56
00:05:44.011 --> 00:05:46.762
I think we're
experiencing time a little differently.

57
00:05:46.763 --> 00:05:48.472
Okay. well. whatever happened. I'm sorry.

58
00:05:48.473 --> 00:05:49.724
I understand. okay?

59
00:05:49.725 --> 00:05:51.309
What? Don't… Don't do that.

60
00:05:51.310 --> 00:05:52.935
- No.
- What?

61
00:05:52.936 --> 00:05:55.438
Don't do the thing that you do
where you try and appease me

62
00:05:55.439 --> 00:05:56.939
before you even know
what the fuck you did.

63
00:05:56.940 --> 00:05:58.816
- I know what the fuck I did.
- Oh. no. you don't.

64
00:05:58.817 --> 00:06:01.527
- Lucky…
- You made me a fucking mark. Cary!

65
00:06:01.528 --> 00:06:03.404
- No. that's not what happened.
- Bullshit!

66
00:06:03.405 --> 00:06:05.072
- I didn't have a choice.
- Bullshit again!

67
00:06:05.073 --> 00:06:06.157
Can I explain myself?

68
00:06:06.158 --> 00:06:07.241
No. I don't wanna hear it.

69
00:06:07.242 --> 00:06:09.160
I know you don't.
but I think you fucking need to right now.

70
00:06:09.161 --> 00:06:11.370
No. I know you've had as much time
to rehearse for this moment

71
00:06:11.371 --> 00:06:12.455
as I've spent picturing it.

72
00:06:12.456 --> 00:06:14.916
So I am sure you've
got a great story loaded up

73
00:06:14.917 --> 00:06:16.375
and ready to go. but I really don't want...

74
00:06:16.376 --> 00:06:17.585
I will hit you again!

75
00:06:17.586 --> 00:06:19.463
Okay. Fuck.

76
00:06:22.216 --> 00:06:24.510
Maybe go for a softer area this time.

77
00:06:25.302 --> 00:06:28.763
Are you seriously trying
to be fucking charming right now?

78
00:06:28.764 --> 00:06:30.264
I'm not. This is hard for me too. okay?

79
00:06:30.265 --> 00:06:32.517
Of course. this is hard for you.

80
00:06:32.518 --> 00:06:34.268
Yes. let's make this about you…

81
00:06:34.269 --> 00:06:36.187
- That's not what I meant.
- …and your obvious misery.

82
00:06:36.188 --> 00:06:37.856
I was terrified. Cary.

83
00:06:38.357 --> 00:06:41.442
Okay? I didn't know
whether I had to be hating you

84
00:06:41.443 --> 00:06:44.946
or grieving you
or fucking somehow saving you.

85
00:06:44.947 --> 00:06:46.615
- I'm sorry. I'm sorry.
- Don't!

86
00:06:48.200 --> 00:06:49.909
You know. at first. I thought that maybe

87
00:06:49.910 --> 00:06:51.619
something had been done
to both of us. right?

88
00:06:51.620 --> 00:06:55.248
Like maybe we were both drugged.
and you were hurt or worse.

89
00:06:55.249 --> 00:06:58.459
and I was gonna have to spend the rest of
my life never knowing what had happened.

90
00:06:58.460 --> 00:06:59.710
But after a while. I realized

91
00:06:59.711 --> 00:07:02.088
that the only possibility
that I could actually accept

92
00:07:02.089 --> 00:07:03.757
was that you were dead.

93
00:07:04.383 --> 00:07:07.343
Because at least if you were dead then
that means that you did not do this to me.

94
00:07:07.344 --> 00:07:10.137
But here you are alive and well
in a fucking beach house.

95
00:07:10.138 --> 00:07:11.431
and you did do this to me.

96
00:07:12.975 --> 00:07:16.644
We've got a hit on the plates and
IDed Masterson at the house in La Jolla.

97
00:07:16.645 --> 00:07:18.521
We've got local cops moving in.

98
00:07:18.522 --> 00:07:21.482
but I'm requesting all federal agents
in the area.

99
00:07:21.483 --> 00:07:24.402
<i>All available units.
report back to the station</i>

100
00:07:24.403 --> 00:07:26.445
<i>to assist an FBI fugitive task force.</i>

101
00:07:26.446 --> 00:07:28.198
<i>Please indicate then switch to four.</i>

102
00:07:28.991 --> 00:07:31.368
Fugitive task force?
Do you think that's him?

103
00:07:31.994 --> 00:07:34.037
We'll know soon enough.

104
00:07:34.580 --> 00:07:35.789
What a mess.

105
00:07:36.748 --> 00:07:38.250
We've cleaned up worse.

106
00:07:39.626 --> 00:07:41.169
Remember Temple City?

107
00:07:41.170 --> 00:07:43.422
Oh. God. I think I blocked that.

108
00:07:43.964 --> 00:07:46.008
The point is. we walked out of there.

109
00:07:47.593 --> 00:07:51.637
You and I have walked out a lot of places
that no one should have walked out of.

110
00:07:51.638 --> 00:07:54.349
Yes. but this is Cary. okay.
He's not like us.

111
00:07:54.850 --> 00:07:56.767
I still have to kill spiders for him.

112
00:07:56.768 --> 00:07:58.061
Drive faster. please.

113
00:08:02.691 --> 00:08:04.609
I know how this looks. okay?

114
00:08:04.610 --> 00:08:07.236
And part of the reason it looks that way
is because it is that way.

115
00:08:07.237 --> 00:08:08.654
I can't deny that.

116
00:08:08.655 --> 00:08:11.199
And I'm not gonna sit here
and try and excuse what I've done.

117
00:08:11.200 --> 00:08:13.994
But I've had some time to think about it.
and even now…

118
00:08:14.494 --> 00:08:16.704
even now. standing here with you.

119
00:08:16.705 --> 00:08:20.124
I don't know if I would have been able
to do things any differently. okay?

120
00:08:20.125 --> 00:08:22.460
And believe me. however much you hate me

121
00:08:22.461 --> 00:08:23.753
right now in this moment.

122
00:08:23.754 --> 00:08:27.048
it doesn't even… it doesn't fucking
compare to how much I hate myself for it.

123
00:08:27.049 --> 00:08:28.966
I think you might
be underestimating me. honey.

124
00:08:28.967 --> 00:08:31.469
- Don't say that.
- Well. I don't know who you are.

125
00:08:31.470 --> 00:08:33.221
- Yes. you do. You know me.
- Cary. no. I don't.

126
00:08:33.222 --> 00:08:34.680
The person I know wouldn't do this.

127
00:08:34.681 --> 00:08:36.641
You're the only person
who's ever known me. Lucky.

128
00:08:36.642 --> 00:08:37.643
Clearly.

129
00:08:40.312 --> 00:08:41.979
Look. I made a mistake.

130
00:08:41.980 --> 00:08:43.232
I know I made a mistake.

131
00:08:43.857 --> 00:08:45.566
But you're not gonna stand there
and convince me

132
00:08:45.567 --> 00:08:47.485
that what we have isn't real. okay?

133
00:08:47.486 --> 00:08:50.112
I fell in love with you
two seconds after I saw you.

134
00:08:50.113 --> 00:08:52.448
- And asking you to marry me...
- Okay. so when did the lies start?

135
00:08:52.449 --> 00:08:53.950
- What?
- Well. was it before the wedding?

136
00:08:53.951 --> 00:08:55.660
- No. That was all real.
- After the wedding?

137
00:08:55.661 --> 00:08:58.287
I know it might be difficult
to pinpoint an exact date.

138
00:08:58.288 --> 00:09:01.123
but I'm just trying to get a general
picture of when my life became a lie...

139
00:09:01.124 --> 00:09:02.501
She was going to kill you!

140
00:09:03.836 --> 00:09:05.878
My darling boy.

141
00:09:05.879 --> 00:09:07.296
Hello. Mother.

142
00:09:07.297 --> 00:09:09.173
- Look at you.
- Hello.

143
00:09:10.425 --> 00:09:11.802
Oh.

144
00:09:13.595 --> 00:09:15.138
Oh. I missed you.

145
00:09:22.479 --> 00:09:23.480
Come on.

146
00:09:25.440 --> 00:09:27.608
I would have visited you if you'd let me.

147
00:09:27.609 --> 00:09:29.944
Oh. I couldn't let you see me in there.

148
00:09:32.781 --> 00:09:35.409
Yeah. I just really hate
that you were in there and not Wayne.

149
00:09:35.993 --> 00:09:37.076
It's okay.

150
00:09:37.077 --> 00:09:38.494
It's not.

151
00:09:38.495 --> 00:09:40.706
Well. listen.

152
00:09:41.415 --> 00:09:45.502
All that matters is I am here now.

153
00:09:46.670 --> 00:09:48.589
Here. sit down.

154
00:09:55.012 --> 00:09:56.013
How did you get out?

155
00:09:56.763 --> 00:09:58.724
Uh. good behavior.

156
00:09:59.349 --> 00:10:00.601
Wayne's lawyers?

157
00:10:04.563 --> 00:10:05.898
What's in it for him?

158
00:10:07.274 --> 00:10:10.527
Well. it's been brought to my attention
that there's some money missing.

159
00:10:18.118 --> 00:10:19.786
Does that have something to do with me?

160
00:10:20.370 --> 00:10:23.247
Well. John's been stealing
from me for years.

161
00:10:23.248 --> 00:10:24.540
Skimming.

162
00:10:24.541 --> 00:10:27.084
And the only person
who knows where that money is.

163
00:10:27.085 --> 00:10:28.504
is that little girlfriend of yours.

164
00:10:30.631 --> 00:10:32.466
- Wife.
- What?

165
00:10:35.052 --> 00:10:36.261
You're married?

166
00:10:37.763 --> 00:10:38.971
You didn't tell me?

167
00:10:38.972 --> 00:10:40.307
You wouldn't see me.

168
00:10:41.350 --> 00:10:42.351
Listen.

169
00:10:43.685 --> 00:10:45.562
I know it's been hard. okay?

170
00:10:46.355 --> 00:10:48.439
You had to do what you had to do
to survive.

171
00:10:48.440 --> 00:10:49.857
But I'm out now.

172
00:10:49.858 --> 00:10:54.695
And we're gonna get our business in order
and everything is gonna go back to normal.

173
00:10:54.696 --> 00:10:56.614
I love her. Mom.

174
00:10:56.615 --> 00:10:58.866
Oh. come on. What happened to you?

175
00:10:58.867 --> 00:11:01.661
I'm gone for two years.
I-I don't even recognize you.

176
00:11:01.662 --> 00:11:04.247
Well. I'm happy. Maybe that's why
you don't recognize me.

177
00:11:04.248 --> 00:11:05.581
- Oh. you're not happy.
- I am.

178
00:11:05.582 --> 00:11:06.667
Look at you. You're bored.

179
00:11:07.751 --> 00:11:11.671
You're working minimum wage
and playing house with that little girl.

180
00:11:11.672 --> 00:11:13.799
You're capable of so much more.

181
00:11:15.884 --> 00:11:17.344
It's a nice life.

182
00:11:17.928 --> 00:11:19.011
- Yeah?
- Yeah.

183
00:11:19.012 --> 00:11:20.638
Is that what you want?

184
00:11:20.639 --> 00:11:21.682
A nice life?

185
00:11:22.266 --> 00:11:24.100
Man. you got a seat at the table.

186
00:11:24.101 --> 00:11:25.893
Wayne is ready to bring you into the fold.

187
00:11:25.894 --> 00:11:29.063
Wayne does not…
Wayne does not give a shit about me. okay?

188
00:11:29.064 --> 00:11:30.815
And he definitely does not
give a shit about you.

189
00:11:30.816 --> 00:11:33.651
Yeah. you bring in that money.
I promise you that's gonna change.

190
00:11:33.652 --> 00:11:35.570
I'm not doing this shit for Wayne. Mom.

191
00:11:35.571 --> 00:11:37.154
No. no. do it for yourself.

192
00:11:37.155 --> 00:11:40.032
I'm giving you a gift here.
This is a chance at a better life.

193
00:11:40.033 --> 00:11:41.242
What. like yours?

194
00:11:41.243 --> 00:11:42.786
You just got out of prison. Mom.

195
00:11:43.996 --> 00:11:45.079
Prison.

196
00:11:45.080 --> 00:11:48.250
I-I-I love that we're having
this conversation right now. I love it!

197
00:11:48.959 --> 00:11:51.086
Look.

198
00:11:51.962 --> 00:11:54.380
Look. you could do it with the girl. okay?

199
00:11:55.799 --> 00:11:58.217
All you have to do is get her
to bring it to me.

200
00:11:58.218 --> 00:11:59.302
And then we're done.

201
00:11:59.303 --> 00:12:00.596
You can live your life.

202
00:12:01.180 --> 00:12:02.347
You know. you can…

203
00:12:02.890 --> 00:12:04.974
move to Fresno and work at Starbucks.

204
00:12:04.975 --> 00:12:07.311
I don't know. Whatever the fuck you want.

205
00:12:09.813 --> 00:12:11.063
So you're saying no?

206
00:12:11.064 --> 00:12:12.399
- I am.
- Okay. why?

207
00:12:12.983 --> 00:12:15.485
I'm in love. Mom.

208
00:12:16.445 --> 00:12:19.113
I'm in love. and I know
you wouldn't understand that.

209
00:12:19.114 --> 00:12:23.075
So you're sacrificing everything
for a girl who is lying to you?

210
00:12:23.076 --> 00:12:24.619
What are you talking about?

211
00:12:24.620 --> 00:12:26.913
That girl that
you're so madly in love with.

212
00:12:26.914 --> 00:12:29.790
You were busted by the fucking feds. Mom.

213
00:12:29.791 --> 00:12:31.668
Yeah. how do you think that happened?

214
00:12:34.880 --> 00:12:36.632
- Huh?
- No. Bullshit.

215
00:12:37.257 --> 00:12:40.134
That's bullshit. okay? Her father
went down in that bust. all right.

216
00:12:40.135 --> 00:12:42.553
So did she. right?
They took her away in cuffs. right?

217
00:12:42.554 --> 00:12:44.889
Yet she was never charged.
never even interrogated.

218
00:12:44.890 --> 00:12:47.808
No. no. no.
Because she was barely involved. Mom.

219
00:12:47.809 --> 00:12:51.103
She was an accessory. Cary.
With knowledge of the organization.

220
00:12:51.104 --> 00:12:52.271
And they let her walk.

221
00:12:52.272 --> 00:12:55.399
Did it never fucking occur to you
to ask her why?

222
00:12:55.400 --> 00:12:57.319
Are you really so fucking naive?

223
00:12:59.571 --> 00:13:00.906
Oh.

224
00:13:07.788 --> 00:13:10.665
Lucky knows where my money is
and you're gonna bring it to me.

225
00:13:13.335 --> 00:13:16.504
You know what Wayne's gonna do to me
if I don't bring him that money?

226
00:13:16.505 --> 00:13:18.423
Are you really gonna let that happen?

227
00:13:19.299 --> 00:13:20.883
Mom.

228
00:13:20.884 --> 00:13:21.969
This is my life.

229
00:13:23.554 --> 00:13:25.722
There was a time
that meant something to you.

230
00:13:28.892 --> 00:13:30.978
You won't do it for me.
your fucking mother.

231
00:13:31.937 --> 00:13:35.231
Do it for your wife if you love her
the way you say you do.

232
00:13:35.232 --> 00:13:38.694
Because you know what happens to her
if I have to handle this myself.

233
00:13:47.369 --> 00:13:50.037
Okay? And you didn't think
to tell me any of this?

234
00:13:50.038 --> 00:13:53.124
Tell you? Tell you?

235
00:13:53.125 --> 00:13:55.668
- Are you fucking kidding me right now?
- Okay. Okay. We…

236
00:13:55.669 --> 00:13:58.129
- Don't turn it around right now.
- Don't turn it around?

237
00:13:58.130 --> 00:14:00.257
You worked with the feds
and you didn't tell me.

238
00:14:01.383 --> 00:14:03.301
You're the reason she went to prison.

239
00:14:03.302 --> 00:14:04.553
They were already on to her.

240
00:14:05.137 --> 00:14:07.513
- Bullshit.
- I had no choice.

241
00:14:07.514 --> 00:14:09.473
When I said that two minutes ago.
you said. "Bullshit."

242
00:14:09.474 --> 00:14:11.143
Well. when you said it. it was.

243
00:14:14.730 --> 00:14:18.483
You can tell yourself whatever you want.
but you know I'm right.

244
00:14:19.067 --> 00:14:20.319
You lied to me.

245
00:14:22.571 --> 00:14:24.447
I wanted to tell you…

246
00:14:24.448 --> 00:14:26.073
- But you didn't. did you?
- But...

247
00:14:26.074 --> 00:14:28.784
You had years to tell me the truth.

248
00:14:28.785 --> 00:14:29.911
Years.

249
00:14:29.912 --> 00:14:32.538
